  "report_period": "Week 23 (29th May to 5th Jun 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Maran Dry Management have committed their \"Maran Argonaut\" 177/2009 SWS, China (SS 09/2029, DD 07/2027, Scrubber fitted) & \"Maran \"Happiness\" 177/2008 SWS, China (SS 06/2030, DD 08/2028, Scrubber fitted) at USD 60 mill enbloc. Remind you that back in March, the older sister vessel \"Lucky Carina\" 178/2007 SWS, China (SS/DD 07/2027) was sold at high USD 23 mill. The Kamsarmax \"Star Moira\" 82/2006 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 07/2029, DD 10/2027, Scrubber fitted) of Starbulk was committed at USD 14,3 mill. For reference, the sister vessel \"Aya\" 83/2006 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 06/2026) was sold back in January at USD 10,8 mill. Furthermore, the \"Key Hunter\" 82/2011 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 12/2027) was committed to Greek interests at USD 20,9 mill, while the sister vessel \"Spirit of Ho-Ping\" 82/2011 (SS 12/2028, DD 12/2026) was sold in March at USD 19,4 mill. In addition, Lavinia Corp committed the \"Themis\" 81/2012 Cosco, China (SS/DD 07/2027) at xs USD 18 mill. By way of comparison, the \"Elway\" 82/2012 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 05/2027) was sold a month ago at USD 16,2 mill. On the Supramax sector, Wah Kwong Shipping committed the \"Tianjin Venture\" 53/2009 Chengxi, China (SS 09/2029, DD 10/2027, Scrubber fitted) at USD 12,2 mill. Note that the \"Planet Team\" 53/2009 Zhejiang, China (SS 01/2029, DD 03/2027) was sold in May at USD 10,5 mill.",
    "tankers": "Scorpio Tankers have committed their LR2 \"STI Broadway\" 110/2014 Daehan, Korea (SS 11/2029, DD 11/2027, Scrubber fitted, \"STI Condotti\" 110/2014 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS 11/2029, DD 11/2027, Scrubber fitted), \"STI Lauren\" 110/2015 Daehan, Korea (SS 04/2030, DD 03/2028, Scrubber fitted) & \"STI Winnie\" 110/2015 Daehan, Korea (SS 03/2030, DD 03/2028, Scrubber fitted) at USD 285,8 mill in aggregate. Remind you that a month ago, their \"STI Park\" & \"STI Sloane\" 110/2014 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS 09/2029, DD 10/2027 & SS 11/2029, DD 11/2027, Scrubber fitted) were sold at USD 65 mill each. The MR1 \"Hans Maersk\" 38/2009 Stx, Korea (SS 11/2029, DD 12/2027) of Maersk Tankers was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 21 mill. Note that a couple of weeks ago, the \"Easterly Jupiter\" 36/2009 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 02/2029, DD 05/2027) was committed at USD 20 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds with redelivery in the Singapore-Japan range were reported between usd 24,000/25,000 pd. A number of Australian trips from North China into Japan were fixed at levels ranging from usd 26,000/27,000 pd. South East Asian trips to China and South East Asia were noticed between usd 20,000/22,000 pd. US East Coast trips to Continent were reported at usd 19,000/20,000 pd. On the period front, Kamsarmaxes were reported fixed between usd 20,000/21,000 pd for 12 months.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "South East Asia trips round trips were reported at a range of usd 17,000/19,000 pd. North China trips into Persian Gulf were reported at a range of usd 23,000/24,000 pd. West Coast Indian trips into East Coast India were fixed at usd 13,000/14,000 pd. South Africa trips into East Coast India were fixed at usd 18,000 pd. Black Sea trips into East Africa were fixed at usd 18,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into West Coast South America were fixed at usd 28,000/30,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Continent were reported at usd 28,000 pd.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "South East Asia trips into US Gulf were fixed at a range of usd 15,000/16,000 pd. East Coast Indian trips from Japan into South East Asia were reported at usd 16,000/17,000 pd. East Coast South America trips into North Coast and West Coast South America were fixed at usd 18,000/22,000 pd."
    }
  },
